# Pairs with AtomicOnOwner. Reproduces #4358 on its own: the routing tier
# places a saga's prepares on whichever copy its cached pair names, ignoring the
# binding, while the flip still waits for the fence. A saga bound to the old
# copy T dispatches k1 through a pair that still names T (mirrored into R) and
# k2 through the resolved copy R only; an undo then swaps back to T and the saga
# decides on T, which holds k1's bucket but not k2's, so a fresh reader sees the
# committed batch torn. SagaBatchOnOneCopy cannot see this: every bucket is on
# the bound copy or the copy it mirrors into. This is the single-defect
# standing check for the router.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerRouterIgnoresBinding
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the routing tier ignores the binding, so part of a bound batch lands only on a copy an undo discards
PERTURBS: SagaPrepare

--- FIND
    /\ LET c == IF p[1] = bound \/ alias = bound \/ BoundMirrors THEN bound ELSE alias
           m == IF p[1] = bound THEN p[2] ELSE CopyMap(bound)
           s == MapOf(m, k)
       IN /\ c = bound
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the routing tier ignores the binding.
    /\ LET c == p[1]
           m == p[2]
           s == MapOf(m, k)
       IN /\ TRUE
--- END

